From: Tiago Damascena <tiagobdamascena@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 17 Sep 2026 10:00:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: rk817_charger: sleep charge credit by current sign, and an OCV recalibration knob

The sleep correction credits "slept charging" only when the PMIC's own
charger was running and its plug-in status is set at resume. On boards
that charge the cell through a separate charger IC and never route the
cable to the RK817's USB input (the R36S: charger state CHRG_OFF and
PLUG_IN 0 in 280 samples of a 2 h charge, 2026-09-16), neither is ever
true, and a charge that happened during sleep is never credited.

Use the sign of the battery current instead, where the PMIC does not
see the cable: at suspend, a positive average current into the battery
is a charge (the rule the status property already applies); at resume,
a positive current read now says the cable is still there. Where the
PMIC does see the cable nothing changes.

Also add a module parameter, ocv_recalibrate (default on), that stops
the rested-voltage recalibration of the columb counter. A calibration
run collects OCV points by sleeping every few percent of counted
charge, and needs the counter left alone across those sleeps; with the
driver built in, /sys/module/rk817_charger/parameters/ocv_recalibrate
is the switch.

Measured on an R36S (RK3326, rk817), 6.12.91.

Signed-off-by: Tiago Damascena <tiagobdamascena@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/power/supply/rk817_charger.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/rk817_charger.c
@@ -18,6 +18,16 @@
 #include <linux/power_supply.h>
 #include <linux/regmap.h>
 
+/*
+ * Bench knob: 0 stops the rested-voltage (OCV) recalibration of the columb
+ * counter, so a calibration run can read the counter untouched across the
+ * sleeps it uses to collect OCV points. /sys/module/rk817_charger/parameters/
+ */
+static bool ocv_recalibrate = true;
+module_param(ocv_recalibrate, bool, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(ocv_recalibrate,
+		 "Recalibrate the columb counter from rested voltage pairs (default: Y)");
+
 /* Charging statuses reported by hardware register */
 enum rk817_charge_status {
 	CHRG_OFF,
@@ -381,6 +391,18 @@
 		1000 * charger->voltage_b;
 }
 
+/* Signed microamps into the battery, read now (positive: it is charging). */
+static int rk817_bat_current_ua(struct rk817_charger *charger)
+{
+	u8 bulk_reg[2];
+
+	regmap_bulk_read(charger->rk808->regmap, RK817_GAS_GAUGE_BAT_CUR_H,
+			 bulk_reg, 2);
+
+	return ADC_TO_CURRENT((short int)get_unaligned_be16(bulk_reg),
+			      charger->res_div);
+}
+
 /*
  * Voltage the gauge latched while the battery was resting. Relax mode only
  * samples below RELAX_THRE_CUR, so this is a true open circuit voltage with
@@ -826,7 +848,7 @@
 	int ocv_soc, charge_now_adc;
 	u8 bulk_reg[4];
 
-	if (!charger->battery_present)
+	if (!ocv_recalibrate || !charger->battery_present)
 		return;
 
 	if (!charger->relax_voltage_uv)
@@ -1360,7 +1382,16 @@
 		return;
 	}
 
-	if (!charger->slp_charging || !charger->plugged_in)
+	/*
+	 * Still charging? Where the PMIC sees the cable, its plug-in status
+	 * answers; on boards that charge through a separate charger IC (the
+	 * R36S) it never does, and the sign of the current into the battery
+	 * is the one thing it knows -- the same rule the status property
+	 * already uses for CHARGING.
+	 */
+	if (!charger->slp_charging)
+		return;
+	if (!charger->plugged_in && rk817_bat_current_ua(charger) <= 0)
 		return;
 
 	moved_uah = charge_uah - charger->slp_charge_uah;
@@ -1401,9 +1432,13 @@
 	charger->slp_boottime = ktime_get_boottime_seconds();
 	charger->slp_charge_uah = charger->charge_now_uah;
 	charger->slp_cur_ua = abs(charger->cur_avg_ua);
-	charger->slp_charging = charger->plugged_in &&
-				(charger->charge_status == CC_OR_CV_CHRG ||
-				 charger->charge_status == TRICKLE_CHRG);
+	if (charger->plugged_in)
+		charger->slp_charging =
+			charger->charge_status == CC_OR_CV_CHRG ||
+			charger->charge_status == TRICKLE_CHRG;
+	else
+		/* No cable at the PMIC: a positive current is a charge. */
+		charger->slp_charging = charger->cur_avg_ua > 0;
 
 	/* Any relax pair found at resume will postdate this suspend. */
 	regmap_write_bits(charger->rk808->regmap, RK817_GAS_GAUGE_GG_STS,
